Question Title-Advanced File Management
Question link-https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/789exi2jqxb0
solution-mkdir project-files
cd project-files
touch report.docx summary.docx draft.docx
cp report.docx report_backup.docx
mkdir old
mv draft.docx old/
mv summary.docx final_summary.docx
cp final_summary.docx old/
rm report_backup.docx
Approach-First i created a directory using mkdir and then navigated into it and used touch to create three files
then used cp to copy paste the content allowing the report.docx to remain as it is
then again created a new directory old using mkdir then moved draft.docx to old/ using mv then renamed a file using mv
then again cp to copy a file into folder and lastly used rm to remove a file report_backup.docx 